9 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111379 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68962" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111379 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $3^{4} \\cdot (3^{2})^{4}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111379 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b41835e6-33fd-5bcf-8a92-0b87adf2022a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111523 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111523 #edb/ref 1061 17217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111523 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e1f34a4c-5543-5841-9a26-631425dd8218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111523 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111524 #edb/ref 1061 17218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111524 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "869d7516-5f01-5ae5-8aa5-fa957c225b74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111524 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111525 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111525 #edb/ref 1061 17336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111525 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "99b9d947-8b7b-5e8a-a9e4-9d2b3a2979a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111525 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111531 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111531 #edb/ref 1061 17999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111531 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8150e1a1-0f41-5dc7-a1db-5e474331d638" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111531 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111884 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's recap some of the rules for exponents.\n\n- **Product rule**: to multiply powers of the same base, add the exponents.\n- **Quotient rule**: to divide powers of the same base, subtract the exponents.\n- **Power rule**: to raise a power to another power, multiply the exponents.\n- **Power of product rule**: to raise the product of two numbers to a power, raise each number to that power, and then multiply.\n- **Power of quotient rule**: to raise a fraction to a power, raise both the numerator and the denominator to that power.\n\nWe can use a combination of these rules to simplify expressions containing exponents. Let's see an example of this." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111884 #edb/ref 1065 3275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111884 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7c442391-b257-5c16-9fe0-292a45e3c172" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111884 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
